    "title": "I&M extends public comment on Lulu-Sorenson project - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Grace Samels ,\n1 hours ago\nALLEN COUNTY, Ind. (WANE) -- After feedback from more than 1,000 residents in and around Fort Wayne about the Lulu-Sorenson project, Indiana Michigan Power (I&M) has decided to extend the window for public comment.\nOn Thursday, I&M issued a press release stating that it will extend public comment after two open houses this week welcomed over 1,000 people wishing to speak their minds on the Lulu-Sorenson Transmission Improvements Project .\nMany landowners, residents, and community members told representatives from I&M at these meetings that they were against the project, especially those as part of the \"No South Route Coalition.\"\nLulu-Sorenson: I&M, coalition on lingering concerns over transmission improvement project More feedback will be accepted through I&M's website, which explains the Lulu-Sorenson project and provides an area to submit a comment.\nThe new deadline to leave a message for I&M is Nov. 13.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "(WANE) -- After feedback from more than 1,000 residents in and around Fort Wayne about the Lulu-Sorenson project, Indiana Michigan Power (I&M) has decided to extend the window for public comment. On Thursday, I&M issued a press release stating that it will extend public comment after two open houses this week welcomed over 1,000 people wishing to speak their minds on the Lulu-Sorenson Transmission Improvements Project . Many landowners, residents, and community members told representatives from I&M at these meetings that they were against the project, especially those as part of the \"No South Route Coalition.\"",
